    "designNotes": "The first roof is joined to the top boundary, preventing a roof ride. The second shelf is too high for the low rebound route; its visible thorned face blocks the ordinary dash-and-climb shortcut. The first patrol is timing-consequential: a saved late departure hits its return. The two different blade heights are a Base lesson, not an advanced launch requirement.",
    "endingForgiveness": "The final loft/dash is part of the challenge. The tested two-frame earlier dash still lands; the receiving shelf is six tiles wide.",
